  note={STRONGLY CONFIRMS: Provider-aware variables are strong monotone/ordinal drivers on LendingClub. Federal Reserve analysis showing "high correlation with interest rate spreads, LendingClub rating grades, and loan performance" and that "rating grades (assigned based on alternative data) perform well in predicting loan performance." Demonstrates that grade-based risk differentiation allows better-qualified borrowers to access lower-priced credit.},
  abstract={We find a high correlation with interest rate spreads, LendingClub rating grades, and loan performance. The correlations between the rating grades and FICO scores have declined from about 80 percent (for loans that were originated in 2007) to only about 35 percent for recent vintages (originated in 2014–2015), indicating that nontraditional alternative data have been increasingly used by fintech lenders. The rating grades (assigned based on alternative data) perform well in predicting loan performance during the two years after origination.}
}

